The Iron Man Mark XLVI (46) suit, featured heavily throughout Captain America: Civil War, serves as Tony Stark's primary armor during the tragic schism between the Avengers. Visually inspired by the "Bleeding Edge" comic design, the suit incorporates miniature miniature arc reactors—known as micro-rt nodes—embedded directly across its limbs, chest, and back, dramatically boosting energy distribution and situational awareness. Built for incredible convenience, it features collapsible helmet mechanics, wrist-gauntlet activations embedded inside helicopter seats, and advanced close-quarters combat algorithms that F.R.I.D.A.Y. used to analyze and counter Captain America's hand-to-hand fighting style in real time.
